                <pb facs="0789" n="705" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg705"/>

                <head>No. 322.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Brigham to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Paso del
                                Norte</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1886-07-22"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 22, 1886</date>. (Received July
                        23.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mexico massing troops at this point: 150 men this morning, and 2,000 said to be
                    on the way. Cutting still in prison. Great excitement.</p>
                <closer><signed>BEIGHAM,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
